<title>UNITED NATIONS: UN okays two more Iraq crude contracts, total 39.</title>
<headline>UN okays two more Iraq crude contracts, total 39.</headline>
<dateline>UNITED NATIONS 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.N. overseers have approved two more Iraqi crude contracts under the oil-for-food accord, putting the total at 39 since the deal's start on December 10, a U.N. spokesman said Tuesday.</p>
<p>As of Friday, there were 37 contracts approved, but overseers granted approval for the latest pair of contracts over the previous two days, the spokesman said.</p>
<p>The 38th contract was a spot cargo involving 1.7 million barrels, while the 39th contract was a term contract for 900,000 barrels.</p>
</text>
